      "hints": [
        "Minimum and maximum observed frequencies occur when the source moves directly away from and directly towards the observer, respectively.",
        "Those positions are half a circular path apart. Find that arc distance, then divide by the constant source speed."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The minimum and maximum Doppler shifts occur at opposite points of the circular path, where the source moves directly away from and directly towards the observer.",
        "The shortest path between opposite points is half the circumference: d = πr = π × 2.4 m.",
        "At constant speed, t = d / v = (π × 2.4) / 12.0 = 0.628 s.",
        "The shortest time interval is 0.63 s."
      ],
